        new("modes", "Your modes and who sees what", [
            "Each connection mode shows only what belongs to it. Your main about appears in a mode only if you turn on \"Show my main about\" for that mode.",
            "Others see a rounded distance band between home cities (for example \"5–10 km\"), never your exact location, and searches are limited so they can't be used to pinpoint you.",
            "We keep versions of what others could see on your profile, so our team can review a report against what was visible at the time.",
        ]),
        new("photos", "Your photos", [
            "Photos you upload are kept private until they have been checked. We remove location and other hidden details (EXIF data) and keep a re-made copy, never the original file. Our own screening service checks each photo for nudity and against databases of known child sexual abuse material (through the Canadian Centre for Child Protection's Project Arachnid, which receives only a digital fingerprint of the photo, not the photo itself).",
            "If the checks aren't sure, a trained member of our team may look at the photo, for a recorded reason that is logged. Photos are stored in our private cloud storage (Cloudflare R2) and shown to others only through short-lived links, only in the modes you choose.",
            "When you delete a photo, or your account, we delete it unless a safety-review retention period or legal hold requires us to keep it. If a photo matches known child abuse material, we keep it sealed as evidence, never show it to anyone, and follow the law on reporting it.",
            "ID verification selfies and documents never go through this process; they stay with Didit.",
        ]),
        new("meeting-safety", "Voluntary meeting safety and trusted contacts", [
            "Meeting safety is optional and free. You can save up to three trusted contacts, including people without Swoovr accounts. Only add someone who is happy for you to share their contact details with us. We keep their contact details encrypted and use them for invitations and safety updates, never marketing. Invitations expire after seven days; contacts must agree before receiving meeting updates and can decline or withdraw.",
            "Incoming contact messages contain your preferred first name, a general status and links, without the meeting time or place. Your selected contacts must verify a short-lived code sent to their confirmed contact details before viewing the read-only meeting summary. It shows your approved, member-provided date, time zone, public venue or general area and check-in status, never the other participant's identity, profile, photos, messages or live location.",
            "We keep hashes of access links, codes and read grants, and minimal consent and notification-attempt records. A protected browser cookie keeps verified read access for at most four hours, within the link's lifetime. This does not sign the contact in as a Swoovr member. Only you can mark yourself OK, home safe, end or cancel the session.",
            "Shared links normally expire at the final expected end plus 24 hours, with a maximum of 30 days from their creation; after home safe, end or cancel, final-status access lasts up to 24 hours unless the link expires or is revoked sooner. Expired links never resume. Ordinary meeting-safety records are scheduled for deletion 30 days after final closure, unless a linked incident, safety review or legal hold requires preservation. Withdrawn or expired contact records have a separate deletion schedule and may remain while required by those records.",
            "Optional after-meeting feedback appears only in your own member features and does not automatically change another person's reputation. It may still be accessed or preserved through lawful restricted safety or legal processes. An incident report can include meeting context without automatically notifying the person reported.",
            "Swoovr does not monitor emergencies or dispatch responders. Missed check-ins are unconfirmed, not proof of an emergency; alerts are not guaranteed to arrive. Calling emergency services opens your device's dialler, and alerting a contact by SMS opens its composer. Opening either does not prove a call or message was sent. An optional location link is explicitly chosen and generated on your device; Swoovr receives no exact coordinates.",
        ]),
        new("text-review", "Text safety review", [
            "When enabled, local automated rules inspect newly submitted profile about text and text messages for limited threat, payment-request, repetitive-message and bulk-outreach signals. These rules can miss harm or flag legitimate conversations and quotations. They do not establish misconduct or automatically restrict an account.",
            "A rule match creates restricted encrypted evidence for authorised human review. Staff decide whether any action is needed; the ordinary account-notice and review pathways apply when a person takes an action. Inspection work is encrypted, and completed processing receipts contain no message text and expire after 30 days unless preservation requires longer. Candidate evidence follows the separate safety-case retention and legal-hold rules.",
        ]),
        new("automated", "Automated decisions", [
            "Some decisions on Swoovr are made, or substantially made, by computer programs using your personal information. Those that can significantly affect you are:",
            "Age eligibility: if the date of birth you enter shows you are under 18, your account is locked automatically. Support can review a lock you believe is wrong.",
            "Banned identifiers: an email address or mobile number that matches an active restriction in our safety registry is refused automatically when you register or change it. A matching legal name and date of birth only goes to staff review.",
            "ID verification: Didit's checks of your document, selfie and liveness decide whether verification is approved, which decides whether you show an ID Verified badge. If the verified date of birth differs from your profile, your profile date of birth stays unverified and you may be asked to correct it.",
            "Photo screening: automated screening decides whether a photo is published or held for a person to review. A known child abuse material match blocks the photo and escalates it at once. Screening never refuses a photo or restricts your account by itself.",
            "Discovery and contact: your filters and other members' filters, blocks, modes, markets, travel and arrival rules, and search limits automatically decide who can see and contact whom. They use your profile, settings (including your gender and Dating \"show me\" choices), home city and trip information, never your exact location or orientation.",
            "Text safety review, described above, only creates candidates for human review. A person, not a program, decides warnings, restrictions, suspensions and terminations. You can ask us about any of these decisions, and appeal an action on your account, through Account standing or the contact details below.",
        ]),
        new("sharing", "Who we share information with", [
            "Other members see only the profile information your settings allow in each mode, and the messages you send them.",
            "We use service providers to run Swoovr, under agreements that limit their use of your information to providing their service to us: Microsoft Azure (hosting and databases), Cloudflare (photo storage and network protection), Didit (ID verification), Twilio (SMS messages, including verification codes), MailerSend (email), Apple and Google (sign-in if you choose it, and push notifications), and the Canadian Centre for Child Protection's Project Arachnid (photo fingerprint matching). If we introduce paid features, payments will be handled by Apple, Google or Stripe, and we will never receive your full card details.",
            "We operate our own self-hosted customer support system using Zammad. Support tickets, correspondence, attachments and relevant customer information are processed and stored in our managed hosting environment. Zammad is not an independent recipient of your information; it is software operated by Swoovr. Authorised support, Trust & Safety, legal and administrative staff may access support records according to their responsibilities and permissions. Email correspondence is also processed by our email service provider.",
            "We may also disclose information when the law requires or permits it: to police and other authorities under our law-enforcement process, to the eSafety Commissioner or other regulators, to prevent a serious threat to someone's life, health or safety, or to professional advisers bound by confidentiality. If Swoovr is sold or restructured, information may transfer to the new operator, who must keep protecting it under this notice.",
        ]),
        new("overseas", "Information that leaves Australia", [
            "Swoovr is operated from Australia. Your account data and photos are stored and processed in Sydney, Australia, including by our support, moderation and safety teams.",
            "To keep Swoovr fast and available around the world, we may replicate copies of that data to data centres in our other hosting regions: Japan and Asia-Pacific (JAPAC), Europe, the Middle East and Africa (EMEA), North America (NAMER) and Latin America (LATAM). Replicated copies are stored there, protected in the same way, and deleted when the Sydney copy is deleted; they are not processed in those regions. All processing happens in Sydney, apart from the providers described next.",
            "Some providers also process information outside Australia: Didit (ID verification) and MailerSend (email) in the European Union; Twilio, Apple, Google and Cloudflare's network in the United States; and Project Arachnid in Canada, which receives only photo fingerprints. Authorities in another country receive information only through the process described under requests from police and other authorities.",
            "We take reasonable steps, including contract terms, security reviews and, where required, approved transfer safeguards such as standard contractual clauses, so that information is protected consistently with the Australian Privacy Principles and any other privacy law that applies to it.",
        ]),
        new("security", "How we protect your information", [
            "We protect information with encryption in transit and at rest, extra application-level encryption for identity records, contact history and evidence, keys held outside our databases, named least-privilege staff accounts protected by multi-factor authentication, and logs of sensitive access that can't be edited. No system is perfectly secure, so please protect your sign-in details and tell us at once if you think your account has been compromised.",
        ]),
        new("device", "Cookies and device storage", [
            "We use cookies and device storage to keep you signed in securely, protect forms and sign-in from misuse, maintain trusted-contact access for a limited time, remember your appearance choices, and remember the country you manually select when viewing Safety & Support information.",
            "Your selected Safety & Support country is stored on your device for up to 12 months so we can show information relevant to that country when you return. You can change your country selection at any time. This preference is not used to determine your physical location, verify your country of residence, or personalise advertising.",
            "We do not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies. Blocking essential cookies may prevent sign-in from working. If you disable or clear device storage, your saved preferences may be lost.",
        ]),
        new("policy-records", "Policy versions and safety updates", [
            "The terms and community guidelines are the operative versions approved for Swoovr. Reading them or signing in does not record acceptance. When an approved version is explicitly required, we record your deliberate acceptance with its version, content digest and server time. Ordinary acceptance records are erased during final account deletion; independently preserved evidence follows its own review and legal-hold rules.",
            "Explicitly published safety updates can appear in your notification centre. The ordinary delivery queue and minimal per-member receipt expire after 60 days, unless preservation requires longer, including when the profile has already been deleted. We keep a version disposition without member or operator identifiers to prevent accidental reuse. These notices do not send email or push. Reading educational safety advice does not create a new acknowledgement or consent record.",
        ]),
        new("appearance", "Your appearance preferences", [
            "We can keep your colour scheme and requested System, Light or Dark display mode with your account, together with a revision, last-change identifier and update time so changes do not silently overwrite one another. This changes only your own interface and is not shown on your profile or to other members.",
            "The browser or app also keeps an account-scoped copy and unsynced choices on your device so appearance can work offline. Signing out clears that account copy and restores the separate guest choice. Conflicting account changes require a choice before replacing either version. Device storage can be unavailable; in that case a choice may last only for the current visit.",
            "Appearance is free. We do not use a scheme to infer identity, gender, sexuality or intentions, or to change matching, visibility, permissions or benefits. Account preferences are included in your own data export and erased at final account deletion; required independent encrypted evidence can remain under the separate preservation rules.",
