        new("beta-access", "Private beta access records", [
            "We keep beta pre-authorisation, activation and revocation records to manage invitation-only access. When enabled, we use your pre-authorised email for an invitation and keep minimal queue, attempt and outcome records; provider acceptance is separate from delivery. Unactivated unlinked records ordinarily expire after 90 days, and revoked records after 90 days from revocation; legal holds or retained evidence may postpone this. Staff may record the status of private iOS distribution work managed outside Swoovr. This is a staff report, not verification from Apple or proof of current access through every other account requirement.",
            "Enrolments linked to your account are included in your own data export and erased from the ordinary account at final deletion. Required independent encrypted evidence can remain under the separate preservation rules. An unlinked or historical access record may need a privacy request to identify and review it safely.",
        ]),
        new("beta-analytics", "Understanding the beta", [
            "When first-party beta observations are enabled, we keep one record per account and UTC day showing authenticated member API activity, whether Explore successfully loaded and whether it returned at least one eligible profile. Activity can include background requests; it does not prove that you read a screen, were online to another member or wanted to contact anyone.",
            "These records contain no filters, mode, intention, location, device or IP information, counterpart identifiers or message content. Authorised administrators can read a bounded internal scorecard using aggregated observations and retained product records, with small numbers suppressed. We do not use it for advertising, member ranking or automatic safety actions, and do not analyse private feedback for it.",
            "Ordinary daily observation records expire after 90 days or with final account deletion. Evidence preservation can retain encrypted copies separately. Missing observations and deleted source records limit what the scorecard can establish; it is not a complete history or a measure of relationship success.",
        ]),
        new("moderation-reporting", "Moderation reporting records", [
            "We keep minimal restricted records of moderation decisions for annual reporting, including the action, its reviewed policy basis and how it was detected and enforced. For account terminations, we record whether your declared home country at the time was Australia, another country or unknown. This is not verified residence. These reporting records contain no message text, contact values or staff free-text explanation.",
            "The reporting schedule keeps these linked records for 36 months, with longer preservation where a hold or retained evidence requires it. We also keep anonymous daily processing totals for 36 months and internal annual aggregates afterwards. Aggregates hide small numeric groups, disclose unknown coverage and do not establish classifier accuracy or completed staff training.",
        ]),
        new("moderated-content", "Text removed after moderation", [
            "Authorised staff can remove an individual profile-text field or a reported text message. Account standing records the action; a removed message is shown as removed by Swoovr rather than as a message the sender unsent.",
            "The exact removed text and the review explanation are kept as restricted encrypted case evidence, including after the ordinary source is deleted. The applicable case-content retention, review and legal-hold rules decide when that evidence can be erased; a separate minimal decision record follows its own retention period. The reporter and internal review explanation are not disclosed through the account notice.",
        ]),
        new("holds", "Evidence we must preserve", [
            "Sometimes we must preserve information, for example after a serious safety report or a verified request from police. A legal hold keeps the records it covers in a restricted, encrypted evidence store, even if you delete your account, while the hold applies and afterwards for any applicable safety-review or police-record retention period.",
            "Holds are reviewed regularly and released by someone other than the person who placed them. Preserving information is not the same as disclosing it. We can preserve only information that still exists; we can't recover information already lawfully deleted.",
        ]),
        new("law-enforcement", "Requests from police and other authorities", [
            "We disclose information to authorities only when the law requires or permits it, after verifying the request, and as narrowly as possible. We tell affected members unless the law prohibits it or it would put someone at risk or prejudice an investigation, and we record why and when we will reconsider.",
            "Information for authorities about how to contact us is on our law-enforcement page.",
        ]),
        new("staff", "Who at Swoovr can see your information", [
            "Our support and moderation staff see what they need to handle reports and appeals. Sensitive records (identity records, evidence, contact history) are restricted to named staff, need time-limited access with a recorded reason, and every view, search and export is logged in a record that can't be edited.",
            "Staff with a known personal conflict are excluded from related restricted reviews. Other administrative access follows separate role permissions.",
        ]),
        new("retention", "How long we keep information", [
            "While your account is open, we keep your information for as long as you use Swoovr.",
            "Customer support records are retained according to their purpose and classification. General Support tickets, including guest and email-only enquiries, are normally retained for up to 24 months after final closure. Ordinary billing dispute correspondence is normally retained for up to 24 months after resolution; financial records are kept for at least 7 years where legally required. Trust & Safety cases are normally retained for up to 5 years after closure, legal and law-enforcement cases for up to 7 years, privacy requests for up to 3 years after resolution, and security incidents for up to 5 years after closure. These periods are subject to continuing necessity, applicable legal requirements and preservation obligations. Information that is no longer needed for a permitted purpose is deleted or de-identified earlier where required.",
            "When you ask to delete your account, it is hidden at once. You can cancel within 30 days of the request until final deletion starts (or ask for deletion straight away); then we erase your profile, messages you sent, identity record and the rest of your personal information, and ask Didit to delete your verification sessions.",
            "When your account is finally deleted, we deactivate and retire your associated customer support account. We remove unnecessary contact details and replace the customer identity with a retired identifier. Some support tickets may remain after account deletion where needed for complaints, financial records, investigations, safety matters, legal obligations or other permitted purposes. We restrict access to retained information and remove identifying details where they are no longer necessary. Retained support records are deleted or de-identified when their applicable retention requirements end.",
            "We normally keep a minimal record that the account existed for 2 years. If the other person keeps their own messages, a minimal reference remains so their history still works; your old sign-in mapping is removed.",
            "Closed police-case records normally follow a seven-year retention period, subject to applicable legal requirements and preservation obligations. Operational backups containing customer support records are retained for no more than 35 days under the standard rolling schedule. Other Swoovr backups follow their separately documented retention schedules, including daily 30-day, weekly 4-week and monthly 12-month schedules. Restored backups must re-apply completed deletions, account retirements and legal holds before the restored information is made available for use.",
            "If your account was terminated, we normally keep its identity record and contact history for 2 years. Active email/mobile restrictions follow the separate review process above. Our retention schedule keeps revoked or expired identifier history for at least 24 months after its latest ending or review, with longer preservation where legally required. This schedule has been approved.",
            "After identifier fingerprints and their history are lawfully disposed, we may keep a minimal record of the decision while the original account ban or preservation duties continue. That record still links to its case and account; it contains no contact fingerprint and is not used to match an address or number. New staff reviews have their own retention period.",
            "Safety-review evidence is normally retained for at least 12 months after the latest completed review or referral where continued preservation is justified. Trust & Safety cases, including serious incidents, normally follow a five-year retention schedule after case closure, subject to ongoing necessity and periodic review. Minimal review and compliance records normally remain for 24 months. Open investigations and applicable legal holds may extend retention. When preservation requirements end, records are reassessed and deleted or de-identified when no longer needed for a permitted purpose.",
            "Customer support system and integration logs are normally retained for up to 90 days, unless needed for an active investigation, security incident or another lawful purpose. Operational helpdesk database backups are retained for no more than 35 days. When backups are restored, we reconcile previously completed deletions and account retirements to prevent information that should have been removed from remaining in active use.",
            "When information is no longer needed for a permitted purpose, we securely delete or de-identify it.",
        ]),
        new("founders", "Founding members' recovery token", [
            "If you hold a founding place, we keep your founder recovery token after your account is deleted so your founding status can be restored if you come back. When you delete your account you can tick \"Also delete my founder recovery token\", or ask support to delete it later.",
        ]),
        new("marketing", "Marketing", [
            "We don't send direct marketing or share your information with anyone for their marketing. If that ever changes, we will ask for your consent first and every message will include a simple way to opt out.",
        ]),
        new("choices", "Your choices and rights", [
            "You can download a copy of your data from Your data and account, correct your profile at any time, choose what each mode shows, and delete your account.",
            "You can also ask us for access to the personal information we hold about you, or ask us to correct it, by writing to the address below. We will confirm who you are, respond within 30 days, and explain our reasons in writing if we can't give access or make a correction, for example because it would reveal another person's information or prejudice an investigation. Access is free.",
            "You can ask us about your information or make a complaint at the address below. We will acknowledge your complaint, have someone not involved in the original matter review it, and aim to respond in writing within 30 days. If you're not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (oaic.gov.au).",
            "If we have a data breach likely to cause you serious harm, we will tell you and the OAIC.",
        ]),
        new("international", "Additional rights depending on where you live", [
            "If the EU or UK General Data Protection Regulation applies to you, RePass Cloud Pty Ltd is the controller of your personal data. We rely on: performing our contract with you to run your account and the features you use; your consent for optional sensitive information, such as sexual orientation and ID verification, which you can withdraw at any time; our legitimate interests in keeping Swoovr safe, preventing fraud and repeat abuse, and defending legal claims; and legal obligations, such as responding to lawful requests. You can ask to access, correct, delete, restrict or port your data, and object to processing based on legitimate interests. You can also complain to your local data protection authority. You give your information directly to us in Australia, and we apply the GDPR to it wherever it is stored. Where an EU or UK provider or hosting location sends your data back to us in Australia, that transfer is covered by standard contractual clauses (or the UK equivalent) in our agreement with that provider.",
            "California: in the last 12 months we have collected these categories of personal information: identifiers (email address, mobile number, account and device identifiers, IP address); personal records (legal name from ID verification); characteristics of protected classifications (age and date of birth, gender, and sexual orientation if you add it); internet or other electronic activity (your activity on Swoovr); approximate geolocation (home city, trips and one-time area checks, never precise coordinates); audio-visual information (photos); and sensitive personal information (account sign-in details, sexual orientation, and the biometric checks Didit runs during optional ID verification). We collect it from you, from Didit, from Apple or Google if you sign in with them, and from other members and authorities, for the purposes described under why we collect and use it, and keep each category for the periods described under how long we keep information. We disclose these categories for business purposes only to the service providers listed above and as the law requires. We have not sold or shared personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising, and we don't knowingly sell or share the information of anyone under 16. We use sensitive personal information only to provide Swoovr and keep it safe, so a right to limit its use doesn't apply beyond that.",
            "California rights: you can ask to know what personal information we collect, use and disclose, and ask us to delete or correct it. You can make a request through Your data and account in the app or by emailing the address below; an authorised agent can make a request with your written permission. We will verify your identity by confirming control of your Swoovr account, respond within 45 days, and won't treat you differently for exercising these rights.",
            "Other US states: if you live in a state with a comprehensive privacy law, such as Colorado, Connecticut, Oregon, Texas or Virginia, you have rights to access, correct, delete and obtain a portable copy of your personal data, and to opt out of targeted advertising, sale and profiling that produces legal or similarly significant effects. We don't do any of those three things. We process sensitive data, such as sexual orientation and ID verification, only with your consent. If we decline your request, you can appeal by replying to our decision; someone not involved in the original decision will review it and respond within the time your state's law requires. If you're unhappy with the outcome, you can contact your state Attorney General.",
